(5550551, 800898, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sprite777:</b></div><hr/><i> Hey - is the noise level here straight out of the cam, or did you use neatimage or something? my d700 is on its way, and i''m stoked about the ISO performance. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>For you and <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=106325" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">and1tricker</a>: I did use a very slight touch of neatimage for this shot, not because of noise, more to enhance the Zen effect. The ISO performance of the D700 is excellent. When I got my D700, I was experimenting with the ISO possibilities and found that ISO 800 is the sweet spot. I wish you lots of fun with your D700 when it arrives - you''re going to love it ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by sprite777: Hey - is the noise level here straight out of the cam, or did you use neatimage or something? my d700 is on its way, and i''m stoked about the ISO performance.  For you and  and1tricker: I did use a very slight touch of neatimage for this shot, not because of noise, more to enhance the Zen effect. The ISO performance of the D700 is excellent. When I got my D700, I was experimenting with the ISO possibilities and found that ISO 800 is the sweet spot. I wish you lots of fun with your D700 when it arrives - you''re going to love it ;-)', '2009-06-30 02:32:41.000000', NULL, 0),
