(5555186, 800970, 31637, '<td valign="top">Found this in the Critique Club section:<br/> <br/>I personally like the cropping, it would make a nice poster. The composition is decent and I think the score is a bit low for this, but probably scored under average because of the negative black space underneath on the bottom of the frame. I love your inclusion of the foliage on the right but the mountains feel hidden to me, and I want to see more of them when looking at this.<br/> <br/>The colors are awesome. I also love the lighting through the dramatic clouds. The photo isn''t bad, just flawed and DPC voters are picky as you probably know.</td>', 'Found this in the Critique Club section: I personally like the cropping, it would make a nice poster. The composition is decent and I think the score is a bit low for this, but probably scored under average because of the negative black space underneath on the bottom of the frame. I love your inclusion of the foliage on the right but the mountains feel hidden to me, and I want to see more of them when looking at this. The colors are awesome. I also love the lighting through the dramatic clouds. The photo isn''t bad, just flawed and DPC voters are picky as you probably know.', '2009-07-02 06:42:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5555188, 800894, 31637, '<td valign="top">Found this in the Critique Club section:<br/> <br/>This is great for the challenge, its simple, and very segregated. Although the subject is hard to distinguish, it feels very alone and separated from everything. I assume its something for birds? The subject isn''t too interesting, but its complimented by a beautiful sky, and exposed very well. I love the tones, and going with a B/W is a good choice, especially since the subject is black. <br/> <br/>Good use of Rule of 3rds, like the sky, but too much water for me. The shadow of the subject isn''t pronounced, so maybe a little bit of a tighter crop would work in my opinion, the water just makes the image dominantly gray.<br/> <br/>I think the image scored well, Id give this a 6. Nice job.</td>', 'Found this in the Critique Club section: This is great for the challenge, its simple, and very segregated. Although the subject is hard to distinguish, it feels very alone and separated from everything. I assume its something for birds? The subject isn''t too interesting, but its complimented by a beautiful sky, and exposed very well. I love the tones, and going with a B/W is a good choice, especially since the subject is black.  Good use of Rule of 3rds, like the sky, but too much water for me. The shadow of the subject isn''t pronounced, so maybe a little bit of a tighter crop would work in my opinion, the water just makes the image dominantly gray. I think the image scored well, Id give this a 6. Nice job.', '2009-07-02 06:50:39.000000', NULL, 0),
